    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0081",
      "sequence": 93,
      "meaning": "Pārvatī says that had the sages met her first she would have placed their teaching upon her head, but she has now offered her life to Śambhu, leaving no room to weigh virtue and fault. If they insist that she must be matched, the playful matchmakers need not be idle, for the world has many grooms and maidens. For millions of births this remains her vow: she will marry Śambhu or remain unmarried. She will not abandon Nārada’s teaching even if Maheśa himself says so a hundred times. She falls at their feet, asks them to go home because it is late, and the sages, seeing her love, hail her as Jagadambikā Bhavānī. Declaring her Māyā and Śiva Bhagavān—the world’s mother and father—they repeatedly bow and depart thrilled.",
