    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0082",
      "sequence": 94,
      "meaning": "The sages send Himālaya to bring Girijā home, then return to Śiva and recount everything about Umā. Śiva is immersed in hearing of her love; the Seven Sages joyfully go home, while wise Śambhu steadies his mind and meditates upon Raghunāyaka. At that time the demon Tāraka, immense in prowess, strength and splendor, conquers every world and guardian, stripping the gods of happiness and prosperity. Deathless and ageless, he cannot be defeated despite their many battles. The gods appeal to Brahmā, who sees their distress and explains that Tāraka will die only when a son born of Śambhu’s seed defeats him in battle.",
