    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0083",
      "sequence": 95,
      "meaning": "Brahmā tells the gods to act upon his advice, trusting the Lord’s aid: Satī, who abandoned her body at Dakṣa’s sacrifice, has been reborn in Himālaya’s home and performed austerity to obtain Śambhu, while Śiva sits in all-renouncing samādhi. Despite the great dilemma, they must send Kāma to disturb Śaṅkara’s mind; then they can bow to Śiva and arrange the marriage. Though Kāma will die, everyone agrees that this is good for the gods’ welfare. At their earnest praise, flower-arrowed, fish-bannered Kāma appears. Hearing their plight, he reflects that opposing Śambhu cannot bring him safety.",
