      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0084",
      "sequence": 96,
      "meaning": "Kāma nevertheless agrees to serve them, for the Veda calls helping others the highest dharma and saints forever praise one who gives up the body for another’s good. Bowing to all, he departs with his flower-bow and helpers, knowing that opposition to Śiva means certain death. He expands his influence and brings the entire world under his control. When the ocean-bannered god of love grows wrathful, every Vedic boundary vanishes in a moment: celibacy, vows, restraints, fortitude, dharma, knowledge, realization, good conduct, recitation, yoga and detachment all flee, while discernment’s army retreats in fear.",
