    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0085",
      "sequence": 97,
      "meaning": "Erotic longing fills every heart; looking at vines, tree branches bend toward them. Rivers surge toward the ocean, while ponds and pools seek union. If such is the condition of insentient things, no one can describe what conscious beings do. Beasts, birds and creatures of sky, water and land fall under desire’s sway and forget all proper time. Blinded and agitated by Kāma, the worlds no longer distinguish night from day. Gods, demons, humans, kinnaras, nāgas, ghosts, piśācas, spirits and vetālas need no description, for they are always desire’s servants; even siddhas, renunciants, great sages and yogīs lose their dispassion under desire.",
